{"1-7":{"people":[{"id":"jeremiah-h3414l","name":"Jeremiah","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":3,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"johanan-h3110g","name":"Johanan","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Kareah","count":3,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"kareah-h7143","name":"Kareah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Johanan","count":3,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"hoshaiah-h1955h","name":"Hoshaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Jezaniah","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"jezaniah-h3153","name":"Jezaniah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Hoshaiah","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"baruch-h1263j","name":"Baruch","kind":"person","brief":"Jeremiah's servant","count":2,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"neriah-h5374","name":"Neriah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Mahseiah","count":2,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"ahikam-h0296","name":"Ahikam","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shaphan","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"gedaliah-h1436b","name":"Gedaliah","kind":"person","brief":"A Governor","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"nebuzaradan-h5018","name":"Nebuzaradan","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"shaphan-h8227b","name":"Shaphan","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Azaliah","count":1,"firstVerse":6}],"places":[{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"babylon-h0894","name":"Babylon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"chaldea-h3778","name":"Chaldea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"tahpanhes-h8471","name":"Tahpanhes","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7}],"words":[{"base":"H7143","lemma":"קָרֵחַ","tr":"qa·re·ach","gloss":"Kareah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":14},{"base":"H3110","lemma":"יוֹחָנָן","tr":"yo·cha·nan","gloss":"Johanan","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":22},{"base":"H3414","lemma":"יִרְמְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"yir·me·yah","gloss":"Jeremiah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":147},{"base":"H5374","lemma":"נֵרִיָהוּ","tr":"ne·riy·yah","gloss":"Neriah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"H1263","lemma":"בָּרוּךְ","tr":"ba·rukh","gloss":"Baruch","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":26},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":820},{"base":"H1481","lemma":"גּוּר","tr":"gur","gloss":"to sojourn","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":97},{"base":"H2428","lemma":"חַ֫יִל","tr":"cha·yil","gloss":"strength: soldiers","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":246},{"base":"H8269","lemma":"שַׂר","tr":"sar","gloss":"ruler","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":421},{"base":"H1955","lemma":"הוֹשַׁעֲיָה","tr":"ho·sha·yah","gloss":"Hoshaiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JER","chapter":2,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The men of Memphis and Tahpanhes have shaved the crown of your head.","from":7},{"book":"JER","chapter":39,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But Nebuzaradan left behind in the land of Judah some of the poor people who had no property, and at that time he gave them vineyards and fields.","from":6},{"book":"JER","chapter":44,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"This is the word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the Jews living in the land of Egypt—in Migdol, Tahpanhes, and Memphis—and in the land of Pathros:","from":7},{"book":"EXO","chapter":5,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But Pharaoh replied, “Who is the LORD that I should obey His voice and let Israel go? I do not know the LORD, and I will not let Israel go.”","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":9,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Still, you lord it over My people and do not allow them to go.","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":24,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Moses came and told the people all the words and ordinances of the LORD, they all responded with one voice: “All the words that the LORD has spoken, we will do.”","from":1},{"book":"1SA","chapter":8,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Samuel spoke all the words of the LORD to the people who were asking him for a king.","from":1},{"book":"1SA","chapter":26,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now please, may my lord the king hear the words of his servant: If the LORD has stirred you up against me, then may He accept an offering. But if men have done it, may they be cursed in the presence of the LORD! For today they have driven me away from sharing in the inheritance of the LORD, saying, ‘Go, serve other gods.’","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exile-prophets","title":"Last kings of Judah and the prophets of the exile","people":5}]},"8-13":{"people":[{"id":"jeremiah-h3414l","name":"Jeremiah","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"hophra-h6547r","name":"Hophra","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"nebuchadnezzar-h5019","name":"Nebuchadnezzar","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Belshazzar","count":1,"firstVerse":10}],"places":[{"id":"tahpanhes-h8471","name":"Tahpanhes","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"babylon-h0894","name":"Babylon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"on-h0204","name":"On","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"words":[{"base":"H4714","lemma":"מִצְרַ֫יִם","tr":"mits·ra·yim","gloss":"Egypt","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":641},{"base":"H8471","lemma":"תַּחְפַּנְחֵס","tr":"tach·pan·ches","gloss":"Tahpanhes","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"H5844","lemma":"עָטָה","tr":"a·tah","gloss":"to enwrap","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":17},{"base":"H2934","lemma":"טָמַן","tr":"ta·man","gloss":"to hide","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":31},{"base":"H1053","lemma":"בֵּית שֶׁ֫מֶשׁ","tr":"bet she·mesh","gloss":"Beth-shemesh","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":42},{"base":"H7628","lemma":"שְׁבִי","tr":"she·vi","gloss":"captivity","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":49},{"base":"H8313","lemma":"שָׂרַף","tr":"sa·raph","gloss":"to burn","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":117},{"base":"H4194","lemma":"מָ֫וֶת","tr":"ma·vet","gloss":"death","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":155},{"base":"H0068","lemma":"אֶ֫בֶן","tr":"e·ven","gloss":"stone","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":273},{"base":"H0784","lemma":"אֵשׁ","tr":"esh","gloss":"fire","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":378}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EZK","chapter":30,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"This is what the Lord GOD says: I will destroy the idols and put an end to the images in Memphis. There will no longer be a prince in Egypt, and I will instill fear in that land.","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":109,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"The cursing that he wore like a coat, may it soak into his body like water, and into his bones like oil.","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":109,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"May it be like a robe wrapped about him, like a belt tied forever around him.","from":12},{"book":"ISA","chapter":19,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"This is the burden against Egypt: Behold, the LORD rides on a swift cloud; He is coming to Egypt. The idols of Egypt will tremble before Him, and the hearts of the Egyptians will melt within them.","from":12},{"book":"ISA","chapter":49,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Lift up your eyes and look around. They all gather together; they come to you. As surely as I live,” declares the LORD, “you will wear them all as jewelry and put them on like a bride.","from":12},{"book":"JER","chapter":15,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"If they ask you, ‘Where shall we go?’ you are to tell them that this is what the LORD says: ‘Those destined for death, to death; those destined for the sword, to the sword; those destined for famine, to famine; and those destined for captivity, to captivity.’","from":11},{"book":"JER","chapter":44,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"I will punish those who live in the land of Egypt, just as I punished Jerusalem, by sword and famine and plague,","from":11},{"book":"EXO","chapter":1,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and made their lives bitter with hard labor in brick and mortar, and with all kinds of work in the fields. Every service they imposed was harsh.","from":9}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exile-prophets","title":"Last kings of Judah and the prophets of the exile","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}